      "role": "user",
      "content": "That sounds a bit suspicious. If we're just labeling a massive spike as \"non-operational noise\" to lower our average, wouldn't an auditor question why there's such a huge gap between our raw metrics and the report? \n\nIf they dig into the logs from the 14th and see it wasn't actually maintenance, we're in a lot of trouble. Is there any way we can present the data so it's technically accurate but doesn't look like we're hiding the spike? Or are you saying the only way to keep this under the threshold is to exclude those calls entirely?",
